N[10]:
  - i: 1765204827529
    n: Supabase customer ID-s
    d: This is a table listing the approved customer ID-s. these function as a password.
    in[1]: uiid
    out[1]: uuid
    img[0]:
  - i: 1765204955660
    n: ID generation script
    d: This is an SQL script that generates a random ID for a certain named customer.
    in[1]: Customer name
    out[1]: uuid
    img[0]:
  - i: 1765205195393
    n: Sign in site
    d: "This is a very basic sign in site with 1 input credential being the uuid\n\nif the entered id is approved, meaning it is contained inside the supabase table for approved id-s, access is granted."
    in[2]: input ID,Supabase table
    out[1]: access granted
    img[0]:
  - i: 1765234763984
    n: Admin Page
    d: "here we can set up the configuration.\n\nOn the admin page for each task we can specify the input variables on the input page.\n\nOn the output page we can load each tasks text (tasks are contained in their own container so this way we can robustly differenciate)\nIn the tasks text we can select showing text part (this is the part we will show on the results site) and inside that we can select part of the text which will be replaced by the specified output variable.\n\nWe can specify output variables with mathematical equations from the input variables for each task.\n\nSummary:\n\nWe specify input variables\nWe specify the showing text part of the task\nWe specify in that part which segment should be replaced by the output results\nWe specify the equations\n\n\n\nWE SAVE THIS ALL INTO THE CONFIG JSON\n"
    in[1]: example task
    out[5]: input variables,showing text,output variables,output variables place,equation
    img[0]:
  - i: 1765234899942
    n: Config JSON
    d: Here we store the configuration data
    in[6]: input variables,showing text,output variables,output variable place,equations,images
    out[1]: config
    img[0]:
  - i: 1765235057400
    n: "examples folder: page"
    d: "\nIn this folder there is a html page of the tasks. here also each task has their associated images if any."
    in[0]:
    out[2]: task text,images
    img[0]:
  - i: 1765235176410
    n: Calculation page
    d: "On this page the user sets the value of the input variables for each task. Each task has its own container, each container contains only the corresponding images if there are any and the input fields for each variable.\n\nMake it mobile friendly!\n\nAfter clicking calculate (only clickable once) the inputs are forwarded to the calculation engine and the results are represented on the results site.\n\nWe autosave every 2 seconds the currently set inputs so if the user quits accidentally, the data is not lost."
    in[2]: access,config
    out[1]: input data
    img[0]:
  - i: 1765235575430
    n: Per user data table
    d: JSON file on supabase to contain all set input data.
    in[1]: input data
    out[1]: input data
    img[0]:
  - i: 1765235643860
    n: Calculation engine
    d: Uses the data from the config JSON to calculate output results from inputs and equations
    in[2]: input data,equations
    out[1]: results
    img[0]:
  - i: 1765235726089
    n: Results page
    d: "after calculation we get redirected here as our further access to the calc page is revoked by clicking calculate. This site is visitable any time infinitely.\n\nUI:\n\nHere for each task we show the showing text defined in the config, with the results inserted to the applicable place highlighted in greeen, and also the applicable picture if any."
    in[4]: results,output place,showing text,image
    out[0]:
    img[0]:
